{
  "id": "nathan",
  "name": "Ch.9 · Nathan's Parable",
  "bg": "radial-gradient(circle at 50% 40%, #241a10, #100a04 65%, #060402)",
  "particle": "dusk",
  "svg": "placeholder",
  "lines": [
    {
      "id": "nathan_0",
      "cite": "2 Samuel 12:4",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "nathan_0_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "The prophet Nathan came to the king with a story about a poor man who had one little ewe lamb, and a rich man who took it from him and killed it for his guest.",
          "position": "middle-left",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "align": "left",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nathan_1",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "nathan_1_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "The rich man had many flocks and many herds. Yet he took the poor man's only lamb and slew it. What shall be done to him?",
          "position": "middle-right",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "type",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "nathan",
          "align": "right",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nathan_2",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "nathan_2_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "As the LORD lives, the man who has done this deserves to die. He shall make restitution fourfold.",
          "position": "middle-left",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "bounce",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "david",
          "align": "left",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nathan_3",
      "cite": "2 Samuel 12:7",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "nathan_3_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "You are the man. You have taken the wife of Uriah the Hittite and killed him with the sword of the Ammonites.",
          "position": "middle-right",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "nathan",
          "align": "right",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nathan_4",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "nathan_4_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "David's mouth went dry. The prophet had not spoken against the king in public. He had spoken to the king in private, as a man to a man.",
          "position": "center",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "align": "center",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nathan_5",
      "cite": "2 Samuel 12:13",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "nathan_5_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "I have sinned against the LORD. Nathan, the LORD has put away my sin. I shall not die.",
          "position": "middle-left",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "david",
          "align": "left",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nathan_6",
      "cite": "2 Samuel 12:22",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "nathan_6_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "The child died, and the king fasted and wept. When the mourning was over, David went in to Bathsheba and comforted her, and she bore a son.",
          "position": "center",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "align": "center",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nathan_7",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "nathan_7_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "The king could have silenced the prophet. Instead he listened, and the broken place became the place from which a new child — and a new song — would grow.",
          "position": "center",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "bounce",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "god",
          "align": "center",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "nathan_7_sfx",
          "type": "sfx",
          "sfx": true,
          "text": "CONFESSION OPENS THE WAY FORWARD",
          "position": "top-middle",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "bounce",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "sfx-impact",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "god",
          "align": "center",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 2
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nathan_8",
      "cite": "2 Samuel 12:24",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "nathan_8_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "The child was named Solomon, and the LORD loved him. Nathan spoke to the boy of wisdom and of a house that would be built without hands.",
          "position": "center",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "align": "center",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nathan_9",
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "nathan_9_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "Teach him, Nathan. Let him hear the truth of what his father was and of what the LORD has made of him.",
          "position": "middle-left",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "david",
          "align": "left",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nathan_10",
      "choices": [
        {
          "label": "Let the story be told honestly",
          "note": "A king who can name his sin is a king who can be trusted with the truth."
        },
        {
          "label": "Keep the failure buried with the dead",
          "note": "Some silences protect a throne. They do not protect a soul."
        }
      ],
      "items": [
        {
          "id": "nathan_10_text",
          "type": "text",
          "sfx": false,
          "text": "David's repentance did not erase the past. It changed what the past would become: a testimony that mercy follows the man who owns his failure.",
          "position": "center",
          "margin": "M",
          "delay": 800,
          "visibleDuration": 0,
          "entryFx": "fade",
          "exitFx": "fade",
          "style": "comic",
          "bold": false,
          "italic": false,
          "rotation": 0,
          "font": "default",
          "fontSize": 0,
          "speaker": "narrator",
          "align": "center",
          "width": "1/2",
          "zIndex": 1
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
